# libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:**   When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT's native `loginViaRemoteUser()` is enabled via the `Setting` model (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). nginx gates `/login` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` header, which Snipe-IT matches against `users.username` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native `snipeit_session`. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (`login_common_disabled = 0`), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "**Usaldusisiku SSO sild:** Kui oauth2-proxy SSO maitse on aktiivne, Snipe-IT on emakeel `loginViaRemoteUser()` on lubatud `Setting` modelli (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`)Nginx väravad `/login` oauth2-proxy/Keycloak ja süstib kontrollitud `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` päis, millega Snipe-IT klapib `users.username` (kasutaja peab olema eelnevalt olemas ja aktiveeritud – sünkroonige need LDAP-i kaudu) vermida `snipeit_session`. Külastajad, kellel ei ole sobivat aktiveeritud kasutajat, saavad vaikselt tavalise sisselogimisvormi. (vigadeta)Parool/LDAP sisselogimisvorm jääb varuvariandina kättesaadavaks (`login_common_disabled = 0`), ja rakendusesisene väljalogimine suunatakse kesksele OIDC lõpp-seansi URL-ile."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-header SSO bridge:** Establishes the owner session from the oauth2-proxy identity (see below)."
msgstr "**Usalduspäise SSO sild:** Kinnitab omaniku sessiooni august2- proksiidentiteet (allpool)."

