# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``, which targets the ``openid-connect/auth`` href explicitly, opens ``/admin``, and signs out at ``/admin/ui/logout``; a second scenario drives the biber-to-administrator mail round-trip across two browser contexts. The path back to the generic personas is a distinguishable login control on Mailu’s SSO page."
msgstr "Mõlemad reisid on kaetud ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``, mis on suunatud ``openid-connect/auth`` Otseselt, avaneb ``/admin``, ja registreerib ``/admin/ui/logout``; teine stsenaarium juhib biber-to-administraator posti edasi-tagasi kahe brauseri kontekstis. Tee tagasi üldiste isikute juurde on eristatav sisselogimise kontroll Mailu SSO lehel."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``: the master-realm super administrator drives the admin console, and the normal-realm administrator and biber each drive the realm account console including sign-out. The path back to the generic personas is an app-shaped surface behind the shared auth chain, which the identity provider by definition does not have."
msgstr "Mõlemad reisid on kaetud ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``: Master-realm super-administraator juhib admin-konsooli ning normaal-realm-administraator ja biber juhivad mõlemad reaalkonto konsooli, sealhulgas sisselogimist. Tee tagasi geneeriliste isikute juurde on rakendusekujuline pind jagatud autentimisahela taga, mida identiteedi pakkujal definitsiooni järgi ei ole."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, which targets the `openid-connect/auth` href explicitly, opens `/admin`, and signs out at `/admin/ui/logout`; a second scenario drives the biber-to-administrator mail round-trip across two browser contexts. The path back to the generic personas is a distinguishable login control on Mailu's SSO page."
msgstr "Mõlemad reisid on kaetud `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, mis on suunatud `openid-connect/auth` Otseselt, avaneb `/admin`, ja registreerib `/admin/ui/logout`; teine stsenaarium juhib biber-to-administraator posti edasi-tagasi kahe brauseri kontekstis. Tee tagasi geneeriliste isikute juurde on Mailu SSO lehel eristatav sisselogimise kontroll."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`: the master-realm super administrator drives the admin console, and the normal-realm administrator and biber each drive the realm account console including sign-out. The path back to the generic personas is an app-shaped surface behind the shared auth chain, which the identity provider by definition does not have."
msgstr "Mõlemad reisid on kaetud `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`: Master-realm super-administraator juhib admin-konsooli ning normaal-realm-administraator ja biber juhivad mõlemad reaalkonto konsooli, sealhulgas sisselogimist. Tee tagasi geneeriliste isikute juurde on rakendusekujuline pind jagatud autentimisahela taga, mida identiteedi pakkujal definitsiooni järgi ei ole."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both layers are process-wide in-process caches. They intentionally do NOT track on-disk file mtimes; CLI tools are short-lived and the assumption \"the on-disk file does not change while my process runs\" holds. The single exception is `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, which writes through and evicts the cached entry for the path it just wrote so a tool that edits a file mid-run sees the new content on the next read."
msgstr "Mõlemad kihid on protsessisisesed vahemälud. Nad tahtlikult EI jälgi kettafailide mtimesi; CLI tööriistad on lühiajalised ja eeldused \"on-disk-fail ei muutu protsessi ajal\" hoiab. Ainus erand on `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, mis kirjutab läbi ja eemaldab puhverdatud kirje just kirjutatud tee jaoks, nii et tööriist, mis redigeerib faili keskel, näeb järgmisel lugemisel uut sisu."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both need the same facts about a role: whether it ships its own container stack, and which deploy modes it supports. Keeping the logic here means the two callers never drift."
msgstr "Mõlemad vajavad samu fakte rolli kohta: kas ta saadab oma konteineri korstnat ja milliseid režiime ta toetab. Loogika säilitamine tähendab, et kaks helistajat ei triivi kunagi."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both on the position"
msgstr "Mõlemad positsioonil"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both paths elevate privileges via `sudo` when not run as root, and the script verifies `bwrap` and `socat` on `PATH` before it exits. macOS uses `sandbox-exec` from the base system and does not need this target."
msgstr "Mõlemad teed tõstavad privileege `sudo` kui ei käivitata juurina ja skript kinnitab `bwrap` ja `socat` peal `PATH` enne kui see väljub. MacOSi `sandbox-exec` Põhisüsteemist ja ei vaja seda eesmärki."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both platforms run model-generated code, which is untrusted, so a kernel-level boundary is required on top of their in-app sandboxing. [gVisor](https://gvisor.dev/) provides that boundary behind an OCI runtime, so each agent app stays a normal container spec and only pins `runtime: runsc`, reusing the existing image pipeline, replicas, healthchecks, and dual-mode machinery. [Kata Containers](https://katacontainers.io/) wrapping Firecracker was the original choice; Decision #2 records why it is unreachable on this container engine. ([E2B](https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra) is the higher-level alternative but brings its own Nomad/Consul orchestration and x86-cloud self-host, which would replace the swarm model.)"
msgstr "Mõlemad platvormid kasutavad mudeli genereeritud koodi, mis on ebausaldusväärne, nii et nende rakendusesisese liivakasti peal on vaja kernelitaseme piiri. [gVisor](https://gvisor.dev/) näeb ette, et OCI käitusaja piir, nii et iga agendirakendus jääb tavaliseks konteinerspektriks ja ainult pins `runtime: runsc`, kasutades uuesti olemasolevat kujutiste torustikku, koopiaid, tervisekontrolle ja kaherežiimilisi masinaid. [Kata konteinerid](https://katacontainers.io/) Restoranid olid algupärane valik; Otsus #2 See näitab, miks see ei ole selle konteinermootoriga. ([E2B](https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra) on kõrgema taseme alternatiiv, kuid toob kaasa oma Nomad / konsuli orkestratsiooni ja x86- pilv isejuhtiv, mis asendaks parvemudelit.)"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both pools feed the assignment, so narrowing `distros` to one value pins every row to it rather than reducing the run."
msgstr "Mõlemad basseinid toidavad ülesannet, nii et kitseneb `distros` Ühe väärtuseni asetab iga rea sellele, mitte ei vähenda jooksu."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both renderers fail loudly when Jinja markers cannot be resolved so generated configs never silently leak unrendered placeholders."
msgstr "Mõlemad renderid ebaõnnestuvad valjult, kui Jinja markereid ei saa lahendada, nii et genereeritud konfiguratsioonid ei lekita kunagi vaikselt renderdamata kohahoidjaid."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both requirement files name the same collections at the same versions: the Galaxy file is the normal source, the git file the fallback used when galaxy.ansible.com is unreachable. A bump that touches only one of them would make the fallback install something the pin does not describe, so an update is applied to both or to neither."
msgstr "Mõlemad nõudefailid nimetavad samu kogusid samades versioonides: Galaxy fail on tavaline allikas, git-fail varukoopia, mida kasutatakse, kui galaxy.ansible.com kättesaamatu. Muhk, mis puudutab ainult ühte neist, muudaks varukoopia installimiseks midagi, mida pin ei kirjelda, nii et värskendus rakendatakse mõlemale või mõlemale."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both run from the trusted workflow ref and check out the version tag for the actual build payload, so the release artefacts match the tagged commit byte-for-byte."
msgstr "Mõlemad jooksevad usaldusväärse töövoo ref-st ja kontrollige tegeliku ehituskoormuse versiooni silti, nii et vabastamise artefaktid vastavad sildiga eraldatud bait-for-byte'ile."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both sides pass `primary_apps` (not the round closure) as the BFS seed and the variant-merged services map for that round, so the reachability walk sees the same topology the inventory baked."
msgstr "Mõlemad pooled `primary_apps` (mitte vooru sulgemine) nagu BFS-i seeme ja selle vooru variandiga ühendatud teenuste kaart, nii et ligipääsetavuse jalutuskäik näeb sama topoloogiat, mida inventar küpsetas."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both sources carry the same pinned collections, so the only thing separating them is how long they take and whether they answer at all. A single slow day says nothing: galaxy.ansible.com degrades and recovers, and a git clone can stall on one runner. The default is therefore retuned only when a rolling window of daily samples shows one source durably behind the other."
msgstr "Mõlemad allikad kannavad samu kinniseid kogusid, nii et ainus asi, mis neid eraldab, on see, kui kaua nad võtavad ja kas nad üldse vastavad. Üks aeglane päev ei ütle midagi: galaxy.ansible.com Laguneb ja taastub ning git kloon võib ühele jooksjale seisma jääda. Vaikimisi häälestatakse see tagasi ainult siis, kui päevaproovide rullaken näitab üht allikat püsivalt teise taga."

# libretranslate
#, no-python-format
msgid "Both targets (Debian changelog and the RPM ``%changelog`` section) are fully regenerated on every run from the kept entries plus an archived-releases notice that points at the documentation site and lists the archived versions and dates as plain text. The notice is folded into the body of the oldest kept entry (not appended after the last entry), because free text after the final entry is not valid changelog data and makes the native parsers warn. Because the package files are regenerated, they cannot drift from the CHANGELOG.md SPOT."
msgstr "Mõlemad sihtmärgid (Debian Changelog ja RPM ``%changelog`` sektsiooni) on säilitatud kirjete iga jooksu ajal täielikult regenereeritud ja lisatud arhiveeritud väljaande teade, mis osutab dokumentatsiooni saidile ning loetleb arhiveeritud versioonid ja kuupäevad lihttekstina. Teade volditakse vanima säilinud sissekande kehasse (ei ole lisatud pärast viimast kannet), sest vaba tekst pärast viimast kannet ei ole kehtiv changelog andmed ja paneb kohalikud parsers hoiatama. Kuna paketifailid on regenereeritud, ei saa need triivida CHANGELOG.md SPOT."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required."
msgstr "Mõlemad tingimused (application_id, service_key) on vajalikud."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required. ``services.<service_key>.name`` must exist in the resolved application config."
msgstr "Mõlemad tingimused (application_id, service_key) on vajalikud. ``services.<service_key>.name`` See peab olema lahendatud rakenduse seadistuses."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required. ``services.<service_key>.name`` must exist in the resolved application config; the stack name is derived from ``application_id`` via the ``get_entity_name`` filter (matching how ``docker stack deploy`` names the stack in ``sys-svc-compose/handlers/main.yml``)."
msgstr "Mõlemad tingimused (application_id, service_key) on vajalikud. ``services.<service_key>.name`` peab olema lahendatud rakenduse seadistuses; pinu nimi on tuletatud ``application_id`` läbi ``get_entity_name`` filter (sobitada ``docker stack deploy`` nimetab virna ``sys-svc-compose/handlers/main.yml``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required; they are validated by `image`."
msgstr "Mõlemad tingimused (application_id, service_key) on nõutavad; need on kinnitanud `image`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both tests route every read through the project caches (`utils.cache.files`, `utils.cache.yaml`); contributors adding a new variable scanner MUST do the same instead of calling `yaml.safe_load*` or `open()` directly."
msgstr "Mõlemad testid viivad iga lugemise läbi projekti vahemälu. (`utils.cache.files`, `utils.cache.yaml`); Uue muutujaga skanneri lisajad peavad helistamise asemel tegema sama `yaml.safe_load*` või `open()` otse."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both the CLI that parses ``--set`` and the inventory manager that consumes the parsed pairs build the key here, so a credential is addressed by exactly one string. A short form would name different credentials on different apps."
msgstr "Nii CLI, mis parsib ``--set`` ja laohaldur, kes parsitud paare tarbib, ehitab siin võtme, nii et mandaati käsitletakse täpselt ühe stringiga. Lühike vorm nimetaks erinevaid volitusi erinevates rakendustes."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both the role-meta lint (`tests/lint/ansible/services/test_addons_schema.py`) and the opt-in external drift checker (`tests/external/update/addons/`) read the constants here so the two layers never drift apart: the lint validates that an addon's declared `mechanism`/`source`/`update.catalog` is one the checker actually understands, and the checker only walks catalogs it has an adapter for."
msgstr "Mõlemad rolli-meta lint (`tests/lint/ansible/services/test_addons_schema.py`) ja opt-in välist triivikontrolli (`tests/external/update/addons/`) loe siin konstante, nii et kaks kihti ei triiviks kunagi üksteisest: lint kinnitab, et addoni deklareeritud `mechanism`/`source`/`update.catalog` See on üks, mida kabe tegelikult mõistab, ja kabe kõnnib ainult kataloogides, millel on adapter."

# libretranslate
msgid "Bounding a service port that carries no access policy of its own, where the packet filter is the only boundary available."
msgstr "Teeninduspordi piiramine, millel puudub oma juurdepääsupoliitika, kus pakettfilter on ainus võimalik piir."

# libretranslate
msgid "Bounds scope; bigger surface to ship cleanly first."
msgstr "Piiride ulatus; suurem pind, et laev oleks kõigepealt puhas."

