# libretranslate
msgid "Every `web-app-*` role MUST include a baseline scenario asserting that the canonical-domain front page emits a `Content-Security-Policy` response header. Roles whose surface is API-only or federation-only (no HTML output) MAY skip this and document the omission in the role's `README.md`."
msgstr "Iga kord `web-app-*` roll PEAB sisaldama baasstsenaariumi, milles väidetakse, et kanoonilise domeeni esilehel on `Content-Security-Policy` vastuse päis. Rollid, mille pind on ainult API- või föderatsioonipõhine (HTML- väljund puudub) VÕIB selle vahele jätta ja dokumenteerida rolli väljajätmise `README.md`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every `web-app-*` role lands on the unified meta + dual-mode contract."
msgstr "Iga kord `web-app-*` Ühendatud meta + kaherežiimiline leping."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every adapter MUST enforce request size, response size, timeout, concurrency, pagination, result-row, and stream-duration limits with explicit values in role metadata. It MUST log provider `application_id`, consumer `application_id`, tool name, credential subject, result status, duration, and correlation identifier without logging credentials or payload bodies."
msgstr "Iga adapter PEAB jõustama päringu suurust, vastuse suurust, aegumist, kokkulangevust, pagination'i, result-rida ja stream-duration'i piire koos rolli metaandmete selgesõnaliste väärtustega. See PEAB logiteenuse pakkujaks `application_id`, tarbija `application_id`, tööriista nimi, mandaatsubjekt, tulemuse olek, kestus ja korrelatsiooni identifikaator ilma logimisvolituste või kasuliku koormuse üksusteta."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every addon of a web-facing role MUST ship `roles/<role>/files/playwright/addons/<addon_id>.spec.js`. There is NO per-addon exemption: no mechanism-based auto-exempt and no `# nocheck` escape; network bridges and auth extensions covered by the role's OIDC/LDAP login spec all ship their own spec asserting the addon-specific behaviour or skip-on-disabled gating. Desktop (`desk-*`) roles are the one exception — they drive no web surface, so they MUST NOT ship addon specs and the lint forbids them."
msgstr "Iga veebisuunalise rolli lisand peab olema laev `roles/<role>/files/playwright/addons/<addon_id>.spec.js`. Puudub iga-aastane erand: mehhanismil põhinev automaatne vabastus puudub `# nocheck` evakueerumine; rolli OIDC/LDAP sisselogimisspektriga kaetud võrgusillad ja auth-laiendid edastavad kõik oma spekt, mis kinnitab lisandi spetsiifilist käitumist või skip-on-disabled gating. Töölaua (`desk-*`) rollid on üks erand - nad ei juhi veebipinda, nii et nad EI TOHI laeva lisaseadmeid ja lint keelab neid."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every agent MUST:"
msgstr "Iga agent peab:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every application role SHOULD follow the same shape: discovery on, the `OIDC.CLIENT.*` endpoints templated, the user identifier read from `OIDC.ATTRIBUTES.USERNAME`, and the scopes limited to what the app actually consumes."
msgstr "Iga rakenduse roll peaks järgima sama kuju: avastus, `OIDC.CLIENT.*` Mallitud lõpp-punktid, kasutaja identifikaator loetakse `OIDC.ATTRIBUTES.USERNAME`, ja ulatus on piiratud sellega, mida rakendus tegelikult tarbib."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every application role corresponds to one Keycloak group whose path is hierarchical:"
msgstr "Iga rakenduse roll vastab ühele Keycloaki rühmale, mille tee on hierarhiline:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every apt suite exists twice, once per upstream mirror. Nexus has no group repository type for `apt` (only maven, raw, docker, yum, npm, pypi, rubygems, go and friends), so the failover lives in the frontend: a request that the primary repo answers with `502`/`503`/`504` is re-run against the `-mirror` repo, which proxies a different host. `404` deliberately does not retry, because a missing file is missing on both mirrors and apt probes for missing files often. The frontend waits at most 8 s for a primary before it re-runs the request against the mirror; the `-mirror` locations keep the global 300 s."
msgstr "Iga apt sviit eksisteerib kaks korda, üks kord ülesvoolu peegli kohta. Nexusel puudub grupi hoidla tüüp `apt` (Ainult maven, raw, docker, yum, npm, pypi, rubygems, go ja friends), nii et tõrge elab frontend: palve, et esmane repo vastab `502`/`503`/`504` esitatakse uuesti `-mirror` Repo, mis esindab teist hosti. `404` tahtlikult ei proovi uuesti, sest puuduvad failid puuduvad nii peeglitel kui ka puuduvate failide jaoks sageli. Kõige rohkem ootab eesrind 8 s esmane, enne kui ta käivitab taotluse uuesti peegli vastu; `-mirror` asukohad hoiavad globaalset 300 s."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every archive file is named `<padded-semver>-<release-date>.md`, where each numeric component of the semver is zero-padded to three digits and the date is the `YYYY-MM-DD` value parsed from the original entry's header. Padded names sort lexicographically in the same order as the underlying versions, so a directory listing is already in chronological order."
msgstr "Iga arhiivifaili nimi `<padded-semver>-<release-date>.md`, kus semveri iga numbriline komponent on kolmekohaline ja kuupäev on `YYYY-MM-DD` väärtus parsitud algse kirje päisest. Padded nimed sorteerivad leksikograafiliselt samas järjekorras kui aluseks olevad versioonid, nii et kataloogide nimekiri on juba kronoloogilises järjekorras."

msgid "Every axis is pinned, so the report is not about what was left open. It is about what each pin rests on: the measurement, the row's own failing combination, or the pool default. A pin from the pool default is a guess, and a green row under it answers a question nobody asked."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every call returns a flat dict with the following keys. Each key MAY be overridden from inventory by setting the matching `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` variable (uppercase, with the `SYSTEM_EMAIL_` prefix)."
msgstr "Iga kõne tagastab lameda dikti järgmiste võtmetega. Iga klahvi võib inventuurist tühistada, määrates sobitamise `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` muutuja (suurtükid `SYSTEM_EMAIL_` eesliide)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every candidate row of the sweep, axes assigned, in global order."
msgstr "Iga kandidaadi rida, määratud teljed, globaalses järjekorras."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every cell carries both directions of one pair, row-to-column above column-to-row, because a bond is declared on the consumer's side and the two need not agree. Brightness is the bond: black for none, white for 1."
msgstr "Iga lahter kannab ühe paari mõlemat suunda, rida-veergu ülalpool veerg-rida, sest tarbija poolel deklareeritakse side ja need kaks ei pea kokku leppima. Heledus on side: must mitte ühegi jaoks, valge 1."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every chunk of the sweep, priority blocks first."
msgstr "Iga osa koristusest, prioriteetsed blokid esimesena."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every client connection MUST map to exactly one provider group named `roles/<provider-application-id>/mcp`. The deployment MAY create or locate the corresponding client-local group by name after startup and then use the identifier assigned by the client API; it MUST NOT predict a generated group UUID."
msgstr "Iga kliendiühendus PEAB kaardistama täpselt ühe teenusepakkuja grupi nimega `roles/<provider-application-id>/mcp`. Kasutuselevõtt VÕIB luua või leida vastava kliendi-kohaliku grupi nime järgi pärast käivitamist ja seejärel kasutada kliendi määratud identifikaatorit APISee ei tohi ennustada genereeritud rühma UUID."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every collector is best-effort: a missing source must never abort the capture. ``INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR`` and ``INFINITO_DNS53_SAMPLER_LOG`` are required and never defaulted here, so ``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` stays the one source. Prints one summary and ALWAYS exits 1 so a failure stays a failure."
msgstr "Iga koguja pingutab kõige paremini: kadunud allikas ei tohi kunagi püüdmist katkestada. ``INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR`` ja ``INFINITO_DNS53_SAMPLER_LOG`` See on vajalik ja mitte kunagi ei ole siin, nii et ``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` jääb ainsaks allikaks. Trükib ühe kokkuvõtte ja alati väljub 1 Seega ebaõnnestumine jääb ebaõnnestumiseks."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every consumer mints its own key and runs the gateway contract"
msgstr "Iga tarbija vermib oma võtme ja kasutab värava lepingut"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every consumer of the legacy oauth2 / oidc service sub-trees, the **OAUTH2_PROXY_\\*** env / Jinja vars, **OAUTH2_SERVICE_ENABLED**, **OIDC_SERVICE_ENABLED**, *oauth2_proxy_cookie_secret*, *oauth2_proxy_application_id*, *ports.local.oauth2*, the dedicated oauth2-proxy provider role, or the legacy *oidc* / *oauth2* Playwright gating helper service names must migrate to the unified **sso** shape. Full plan and decisions are archived under req 21."
msgstr "Iga pärandvara tarbija2 / oidc teenuse alampuud, **OAUTH2_PROXY_\\*** env / Jinja vars, **OAUTH2_SERVICE_ENABLED**, **OIDC_SERVICE_ENABLED**, *oauth2_proxy_cookie_secret*, *oauth2_proxy_application_id*, *ports.local.oauth2*,2volitatud esindaja roll või pärand *Oidc* / *Oauth2* Playwrighti gating abistaja teenuse nimed peavad rändama ühtsesse **Sso** kuju. Kogu plaan ja otsused arhiveeritakse req 21."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every consumer speaks only the gateway `/v1`; the gateway is the single place backends are wired."
msgstr "Iga tarbija räägib ainult väravast `/v1`; värav on üks koht, kus taustaprogrammid on traadiga."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every declared backend has a `model_list` branch"
msgstr "Igal deklareeritud taustaprogrammil on `model_list` haru"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every declared distro id, in declaration order."
msgstr "Iga deklareeritud distro ID deklaratsiooni järjekorras."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every deploy mode a role's primary entity may toggle. ``compose``/``swarm`` target stack roles (own container stack); ``host`` targets invokable roles that configure the host instead of shipping a stack."
msgstr "Igas juurutamisrežiimis võib rolli põhiolemus lülituda. ``compose``/``swarm`` sihtmärgi stack rollid (oma konteinerikorstna); ``host`` sihib väljakutsutavaid rolle, mis konfigureerivad hosti, selle asemel et saata virna."

msgid "Every deploy opens with a `=== compose-deploy:` line listing the arguments it actually resolved. Read it instead of trusting the command you typed: rewriting `apps=` is where `disable=` and `full_cycle=` get lost, and the line shows what is missing before the play starts."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every discovered endpoint authenticates through a header. A provider that keys its session by URL segment instead cannot scope that segment per consumer or revoke it, so it is fronted by an adapter and the segment stays between the adapter and its upstream."
msgstr "Iga avastatud lõpp-punkt autentitakse päise kaudu. Selle asemel ei saa pakkuja, kes võtmeb oma seansi URL-segmendi järgi, seda segmenti tarbija kohta laiendada ega tühistada, nii et see on adapteri ees ja segment jääb adapteri ja selle ülesvoolu vahele."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every embodiable agent runs the admission checks"
msgstr "Iga kehaline agent kontrollib sissepääsu"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every emoji used as a STRUCTURED marker across the project (complexity-matrix columns, lifecycle stages, deploy modes, boolean/state cells) is defined here exactly once, so a glyph means the same thing everywhere it appears. Emojis are unique: the module fails to import if two words share a glyph."
msgstr "Iga emoji, mida kasutatakse projektis struktureeritud markerina (keerukus-maatrikskolonnid, elutsükli etapid, kasutusrežiimid, tõeväärtus-/olekurakud) See on siin täpselt üks kord määratletud, nii et glüüf tähendab sama asja kõikjal, kus see ilmub. Emojid on unikaalsed: moodul ei impordi, kui kaks sõna jagavad glüüfi."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every env variable the spec reads MUST be exposed in the role's `templates/playwright.env.j2`. Names MUST match exactly."
msgstr "Iga env muutuja, mida spekter loeb, PEAB olema rollis `templates/playwright.env.j2`. Nimed peavad täpselt vastama."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every exposed provider remains a separate logical MCP server even when a common proxy implementation serves it. This preserves the mapping between `roles/<provider-application-id>/mcp`, the client connection, the upstream credential, the tool allowlist, and the audit record."
msgstr "Iga avatud pakkuja jääb eraldi loogiliseks MCP-serveriks isegi siis, kui seda teenib ühine puhverserver. See säilitab kaardistamise `roles/<provider-application-id>/mcp`, kliendiühendust, eelnevat volitust, tööriista lubamisnimekirja ja auditi kirjet."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every external CI trigger MUST route through one of the entry workflows. Each entry translates its event into a call to the orchestrator; the catalog of triggers and inputs lives in [workflows.md](../../tools/github/actions/workflows.md)."
msgstr "Iga väline CI käivitaja PEAB läbima ühe sisenemise töövoo. Iga sissekanne tõlgib oma sündmuse orkestraatorile kõneks; käivitajate ja sisendite kataloog elab [workflows.md](../../tools/github/actions/workflows.md)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every external test directory MUST contain `__init__.py` so repository-wide test structure checks keep passing."
msgstr "Iga väline testkataloog peab sisaldama `__init__.py` nii et kogu hoidlat hõlmavad teststruktuuri kontrollid läbivad."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every failure is fixed at its root. A lint hit is resolved by deleting the offending construct, not by a `nocheck` marker, a loosened rule, or a target dropped from the gate — any suppression needs the operator's explicit approval and a stated reason."
msgstr "Iga ebaõnnestumine on fikseeritud oma juure. Lint tabamus lahendatakse rikkuva konstruktsiooni kustutamisega, mitte `nocheck` marker, lõdvendatud reegel või väravast välja visatud sihtmärk – igasugune väljatõrjumine vajab operaatori selgesõnalist heakskiitu ja põhjendust."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every failure raises AnsibleError with an actionable message."
msgstr "Iga ebaõnnestumine tõstab AnsibleError'i käivitatava sõnumiga."

msgid "Every file here is declared as an addon under `meta/addons/` with `mechanism: mu_plugin` and `source: vendored`, and the addon id is the file stem. [04_mu_plugins.yml](../../tasks/04_mu_plugins.yml) loops over those declarations and copies `<addon_id>.php` into the container on every deploy; a new file therefore needs its `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml` entry and a Playwright spec before it is installed."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every handler module MUST expose the same surface so the registry can call it uniformly:"
msgstr "Iga käitleja moodul PEAB avama sama pinna, et register saaks seda ühtlaselt nimetada:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every input the run named *title* records, keyed by input name."
msgstr "Iga käivitatud sisendi nimi *tiitli* kirjed, mis on sisestatud nimega."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every input the source run was dispatched with, except the selection."
msgstr "Kõik sisendid, millega lähtekoodi käivitati, välja arvatud valik."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every install is best-effort and per-command: cross-distro tools are often unavailable, and ``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` skips absent ones, so a failed candidate MUST NOT break the lint bootstrap. The validators are intentionally kept out of the install stamp's required-tool set so a non-Debian environment never loops trying to install a tool it cannot. This group is installed explicitly by the ``lint-packages`` make target (an explicit group bypasses the stamp), so the commands are provisioned every run rather than only on the first all-mode install."
msgstr "Iga installimine on parim pingutus ja käsk: ristdistro tööriistad on sageli kättesaamatud ja ``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` Puudub, nii et ebaõnnestunud kandidaat ei tohi lõhkuda lint bootstrap. Valideerijaid hoitakse tahtlikult installimargi nõutud tööriistakomplektist välja, nii et mitte-Debian keskkond ei püüa kunagi tööriista installida. See grupp on installitud selgesõnaliselt ``lint-packages`` sihtmärgiks (selge rühm möödub templist), nii et käske pakutakse igal käivitamisel, mitte ainult esimesel täisrežiimil installimisel."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every installable package is declared exactly once, in one of two places:"
msgstr "Iga paigaldatav pakett deklareeritakse täpselt üks kord, ühes kahest kohast:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every invokable role in the tested lifecycle envelope, with its upstream homepage, an introduction video, the roles it integrates with, and a one-command local install."
msgstr "Iga väljakutsuv roll testitud elutsükli ümbrises, selle ülesvoolu koduleht, sissejuhatav video, rollid, millega see integreerub, ja ühe käsu kohalik install."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every key MUST be the fully qualified form :func:`override_key` builds; a short form is rejected rather than guessed at, because the same short key names different credentials on different apps."
msgstr "Iga võti peab olema täielikult kvalifitseeritud vorm. :func:`override_key` ehitab; lühike vorm lükatakse tagasi, mitte arvatakse, sest samad lühikesed võtmed nimetavad erinevaid volitusi erinevates rakendustes."

msgid "Every line of the file named by ``ANSIBLE_LOG_PATH`` carries ``<ts> p=<pid> u=<user> n=<name> <LEVEL>|`` and a space in front of the message that also went to stdout. Left unstripped, that prefix defeats every line-anchored matcher a reader applies, so a reader that mixes an anchored match with an unanchored one silently sees an empty log instead of failing."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every literal a rendered segment can start with, so any of them ends the value before it."
msgstr "Iga sõnasõnaline renderdatud segment võib alata, nii et iga neist lõpeb väärtus enne seda."

msgid "Every matrix variant overrides the sample count to 1. At that setting the single sample is kept rather than discarded as cold, because what a CI round proves is that the measurement, the store and the re-render ran, not what the rate was on a shared runner."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every mode is read; there is no scope to narrow to. A run that failed in swarm and in compose comes back as two tokens for the same role."
msgstr "Iga režiim loetakse; ei ole ruumi kitsendada. Jooks, mis ebaõnnestus sülemis ja kompositsioonis, tuleb tagasi kahe märgina sama rolli jaoks."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Every model LiteLLM publishes, as ``{alias, params, context, traits}``."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every module here SHOULD expose a callable function for in-process use and a `__main__` shim so the same code path is reachable from shell orchestrators via `python -m utils.cleanup.<module>`."
msgstr "Igas moodulis PEAKS olema väljakutsutav funktsioon protsessisiseseks kasutamiseks ja `__main__` Shim nii, et sama kooditee on kättesaadav shelliorkestrite kaudu `python -m utils.cleanup.<module>`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every non-empty body line gets a ``- `` continuation prefix so rpm does not read a markdown ``*`` bullet at column 0 as a new changelog entry header (which makes ``rpmspec`` report ``bad date``). Blank lines stay blank. *footer_md* (the archived-releases notice) is folded into this entry's body for the same reason it is on the Debian side: trailing free text confuses the parser."
msgstr "Iga mittetühi kehaliin saab ``- `` jätkuprefiks, nii et rpm ei loe markdowni ``*`` kolonnikuul 0 uue muudatuste logikirje päisena (teeb ``rpmspec`` raport ``bad date``). Tühjad jooned jäävad tühjaks. *footer_md* (arhiveeritud vabastamise teatis) on volditud selle kirje kehasse samal põhjusel, miks see on Debiani poolel: vaba teksti jälitamine ajab parser segadusse."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every non-empty line of the markdown body gets a two-space indent so Debian's parser accepts it: each change line MUST start with at least two spaces, otherwise dpkg treats it as a badly formatted line, loses the entry boundary and reports an empty maintainer. Blank lines stay blank."
msgstr "Iga mittetühi rida markdown keha saab kahe tühikuga taande, nii et Debiani parser aktsepteerib seda: iga muutus rida PEAB algama vähemalt kahe tühikuga, vastasel juhul käsitleb dpkg seda halvasti vormindatud reana, kaotab sisenemise piiri ja teatab tühjast hooldajast. Tühjad jooned jäävad tühjaks."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every one of them needs the same four things before it can call into :mod:`utils.networks.render`: the resolved variables, the deployment mode, a service registry built from the merged applications, and closures over the ``config`` and ``database`` lookups. Building that once means a change to how the registry or the closures are obtained cannot reach one lookup and miss another."
msgstr "Igaüks neist vajab samu asju, enne kui ta saab helistada. :mod:`utils.networks.render`: lahendatud muutujad, kasutuselevõtu viis, ühendatud rakendustest ehitatud teenuseregister ja sulgemised ``config`` ja ``database`` otsinguid. Hoone, mis kord tähendab registri või sulgemiste saamise viisi muutust, ei saa ühe otsinguni jõuda ja teise vahele jätta."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every other agent deployment in [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md) keeps the agent kernel-isolated. This role is the deliberate inverse defined by [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md) Decision #12 (embodied / dedicated-device mode): for a robot, the useful trust boundary is the **whole device**, because the agent's job is to drive that device's hardware (GPIO, I2C/SPI sensors, cameras, actuators, motors). A microVM around the agent would only get in the way of the very hardware it is meant to control."
msgstr "Kõik teised agendid [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md) hoiab aine tuuma isoleerituna. See roll on tahtlik pöördväärtus, mida defineerib [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md) Otsus #12 (sisseehitatud/eriseadme režiim)Roboti jaoks on kasulik usalduse piir **terve seade**, sest agendi ülesanne on juhtida selle seadme riistvara (GPIO, ma2C/SPI andurid, kaamerad, ajamid, mootorid)MikroVM agendi ümber takistaks ainult seda riistvara, mida see peaks kontrollima."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every page carries a version switcher in its sidebar. Switching keeps the current page and falls back to the start page of a version that lacks it."
msgstr "Igal lehel on külgribal versioonilüliti. Lülitamine hoiab aktiivset lehte ja langeb tagasi versiooni alguslehele, millel see puudub."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every path either deploys on the assigned kind, reports the substitution, or fails. None of them substitutes in silence."
msgstr "Iga rada kas kasutab määratud liiki, teatab asendusest või ebaõnnestub. Ükski neist ei asenda vaikides."

msgid "Every path that cannot route rejects the request with its reason instead of answering. The hook returns a string when the proxy has no router or when no served model can take the request, and the proxy turns that into a `RejectedRequestError` carrying the text. The alias's own `model_list` entry exists only so the name is listable and carries `mock_response: litellm.InternalServerError`, so reaching it at all raises. Both halves matter, because a router that silently served whatever was first would hide its own failure behind a plausible reply, and the alias exists precisely so callers do not have to know which model answered."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every per-tool module MUST expose the same surface so the dispatcher can call it uniformly:"
msgstr "Iga töövahendi moodul PEAB avama sama pinna, et dispetšer saaks seda ühtlaselt nimetada:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every persona scenario MUST run the CSP injection assertion at least once on the role's canonical surface. When an injector service (`asset`, `cdn`, `css`, `javascript`, `simpleicons`, `matomo`) is enabled, the page's `Content-Security-Policy` header MUST list the injector's host. The assertion is centralised in [`personas/utils/csp.js`](../../../../../roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/personas/utils/csp.js) so every spec gets the check by default."
msgstr "Iga persona-stsenaarium PEAB käivitama CSP-süstimise kinnituse vähemalt üks kord rolli kanoonilisel pinnal. Injektori kasutamisel (`asset`, `cdn`, `css`, `javascript`, `simpleicons`, `matomo`) on lubatud, lehekülje `Content-Security-Policy` Päisel PEAB olema kirjas injektori host. Väide on tsentraliseeritud [`personas/utils/csp.js`](../../../../../roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/personas/utils/csp.js) Nii et iga spetsifikatsioon saab vaikimisi kontrolli."

msgid "Every plugin and mu-plugin is declared in ``meta/addons/`` under the unified addon contract. The OIDC and WP-Discourse runtime config lives in each addon’s ``config:`` block. Both install paths read those declarations: a ``required`` addon that fails to install stops the deploy, an optional one warns and is skipped."
msgstr ""

msgid "Every plugin and mu-plugin is declared in `meta/addons/` under the unified addon contract. The OIDC and WP-Discourse runtime config lives in each addon's `config:` block. Both install paths read those declarations: a `required` addon that fails to install stops the deploy, an optional one warns and is skipped."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every probe here targets the container's own loopback, so a request that a proxy picks up is wrong by definition -- the Wget probe has said so with ``--proxy=off`` since it was written. Both spellings come from here so the exec form and the shell form cannot drift: the shell form needs the wildcard quoted and the exec form needs it bare, which is exactly the kind of difference that rots when it is written out three times."
msgstr "Iga sond siin sihib konteineri enda tagasilööki, nii et taotlus, mille proxy kiirendab, on määratluse järgi vale - Wget'i sond on seda öelnud ``--proxy=off`` kuna see oli kirjutatud. Mõlemad kirjapildid pärinevad siit, nii et exec-vorm ja shellivorm ei saa triivida: shellivorm vajab tsiteeritud metamärki ja exec-vorm vajab seda paljaks, mis on täpselt selline erinevus, mis mädaneb, kui see on kolm korda välja kirjutatud."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every push runs the same gate you can run locally:"
msgstr "Iga tõukega jookseb sama värav, mida saab kohapeal käivitada:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every reason the tokens of one input cannot deploy on this branch."
msgstr "Igal põhjusel ei saa ühe sisendi märgid sellel harul rakendada."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every rejected entry carries a stable `reason`: `consumer_not_allowed`, `transport_unsupported`, `auth_unsupported`, `credential_missing` or `endpoint_unreachable`."
msgstr "Iga tagasilükatud sissekanne kannab stabiilset `reason`: `consumer_not_allowed`, `transport_unsupported`, `auth_unsupported`, `credential_missing` või `endpoint_unreachable`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every replica serves from the shared ``docs_sites`` volume. The replica holding ``builder.lock`` in that volume fetches and builds; the queue (``queue/``) and the build states (``states/``) are files beside the sites, so a new lock holder resumes the queue when the builder dies. Cross-node locking relies on NFSv4, the default of ``svc-storage-nfs-client``."
msgstr "Iga koopia teenib jagatud ``docs_sites`` maht. Järelproovi pidamine ``builder.lock`` Selles mahus tõmbab ja ehitab; järjekord (``queue/``) ja ehitusriigid (``states/``) on failid saitide kõrval, nii et uus lukuhoidja jätkab järjekorda, kui ehitaja sureb. Ristsõlme lukustamine tugineb NFSv-le4, ``svc-storage-nfs-client``."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every replica serves from the shared `docs_sites` volume. The replica holding `builder.lock` in that volume fetches and builds; the queue (`queue/`) and the build states (`states/`) are files beside the sites, so a new lock holder resumes the queue when the builder dies. Cross-node locking relies on NFSv4, the default of `svc-storage-nfs-client`."
msgstr "Iga koopia teenib jagatud `docs_sites` maht. Järelproovi pidamine `builder.lock` Selles mahus tõmbab ja ehitab; järjekord (`queue/`) ja ehitusriigid (`states/`) on failid saitide kõrval, nii et uus lukuhoidja jätkab järjekorda, kui ehitaja sureb. Ristsõlme lukustamine tugineb NFSv-le4, `svc-storage-nfs-client`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every requirements file MUST follow the pattern `NNN-topic.md`, where `NNN` is a zero-padded three-digit sequence number (e.g. `000-template.md`, `001-auth.md`)."
msgstr "Iga nõude fail peab järgima mustrit `NNN-topic.md`, kus `NNN` on nullpaddded kolmekohaline järjenumber (nt. `000-template.md`, `001-auth.md`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every requirements file MUST follow this template exactly:"
msgstr "Iga nõuete fail peab järgima seda malli täpselt:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every role MUST declare its Docker images in `meta/services.yml`. The file root IS the services map keyed by `<service-name>` (no `compose:` and no `services:` wrapper):"
msgstr "Iga roll peab deklareerima oma Dockeri pildid `meta/services.yml`. Faili juur IS teenuste kaart, mille võtmeks on `<service-name>` (ei `compose:` ja ei `services:` ümbris):"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every role file with its per-type policy and dotted-path entries."
msgstr "Iga rollifail oma tüübireeglite ja punktiirjoone kirjetega."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every role that declares RBAC at the file root of its `meta/rbac.yml` MUST be provisioned with a per-application namespace under the container named by `RBAC.GROUP.NAME` (default `roles`). Each LDAP group entry is a direct child of that container; the application identifier (and the tenant identifier, if any) is encoded into the CN with hyphen separators:"
msgstr "Iga roll, mis deklareerib RBAC- i selle failijuures `meta/rbac.yml` PEAVAD olema varustatud ühe rakenduse nimeruumiga konteineri all, mille nimi on `RBAC.GROUP.NAME` (vaikimisi `roles`). Iga LDAP grupi kirje on selle konteineri otsene laps; rakenduse identifikaator (ja rentniku tunnus, kui see on olemas) kodeeritakse CNi sidekriipsu eraldajatega:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every role that ships role-level extensions MUST declare them under `roles/<role>/meta/addons/`, one file per addon at `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml`. The file root IS the addon spec; there is NO wrapping `<addon_id>:` key (the filename stem supplies the addon id)."
msgstr "Iga roll, mis saadab rollitaseme laiendusi, peab neid deklareerima `roles/<role>/meta/addons/`, üks fail addoni kohta `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml`. Faili juur ON addon spec; ümbrist ei ole `<addon_id>:` võti (failinime tüvi varustab lisandi ID- ga)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every role type with the files it MAY or MUST ship."
msgstr "Iga rollitüüp koos failidega võib või peab saatma."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every role with an ``application_id`` declares exactly one ``mcp:`` entry. The block is an audit disposition first and a deployable surface second: ``classification`` states what the role is, and only a deployable classification may also carry ``enabled``/``shared`` and a served contract."
msgstr "Iga roll koos ``application_id`` kuulutab täpselt ühe ``mcp:`` sissepääs. Plokk on kõigepealt auditi dispositsioon ja teisena rakendatav pind: ``classification`` näitab, mis roll on, ja ainult kasutatav klassifikatsioon võib kanda ka ``enabled``/``shared`` ja teenindatud leping."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every role with an `application_id` MUST contain one role-local `mcp:` audit mapping in `meta/services.yml`. This requirement supersedes requirement 025's rule that absence means no upstream path, because absence cannot distinguish a reviewed refusal from a role that nobody examined. Discovery MUST select only a deployable classification with explicit `enabled: true` and `shared: true`; audit-only mappings MUST never become endpoints."
msgstr "Iga roll koos `application_id` PEAB sisaldama ühte kohalikku rolli `mcp:` auditi kaardistamine `meta/services.yml`. See nõue asendab nõuet . 025Reegel, et puudumine ei tähenda ülesvoolu, sest puudumine ei saa eristada läbivaadatud keeldumist rollist, mida keegi ei uurinud. Discovery PEAB valima ainult ekspluateeritava klassifikatsiooni `enabled: true` ja `shared: true`; ainult auditiga seotud kaardistamised ei tohi kunagi muutuda lõpp-punktideks."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every row is assigned its deploy mode, tor state, distro, filesystem and CPU architecture by its position in that list (:mod:`utils.github.variant.axes`)."
msgstr "Igale reale on omistatud selle kasutusrežiim, tor olek, distro, failisüsteem ja CPU arhitektuur vastavalt selle positsioonile nimekirjas. (:mod:`utils.github.variant.axes`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every row of the CI matrix is one ``role#variant`` selection. Five axes are decided here, all as a deterministic rotation over the row's position in the *global* discovery order and the sweep number -- never at random, so a red job can be reproduced by re-running the same sweep, and so consecutive sweeps cover the combinations instead of sampling them:"
msgstr "Iga CI maatriksi rida on üks ``role#variant`` valik. Siin otsustatakse viis telge, kõik deterministliku pöörlemisena üle rea asendi *globaalse* avastusjärjekord ja pühkimisnumber - mitte kunagi juhuslikult, nii et punast tööd saab reprodutseerida sama pühkimise uuesti käivitamisega ja nii katavad järjestikused pühkimised kombinatsioone nende proovide võtmise asemel:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every rule in `permissions.ask` assumes the operator reads the prompt and confirms the action matches intent. Rules in `ask` are NOT a hard barrier. They are a speed-bump that converts automatic execution into a deliberate decision."
msgstr "Iga reegel `permissions.ask` eeldab, et operaator loeb päringut ja kinnitab tegevuse kavatsust. Reeglid `ask` See ei ole kõva barjäär. Need on kiirusmõõt, mis muudab automaatse täitmise teadlikuks otsuseks."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every runner instance is an ephemeral container that mounts its host's docker socket (DooD). For each CI job it starts a fresh Infinito DinD container with a unique subnet and volume, runs the job inside it, and tears it down; the runner then re-registers with GitHub as a fresh ephemeral runner."
msgstr "Iga jooksja eksemplar on üürike konteiner, mis paigaldab oma võõrustaja dokkimispesa. (DooD). Iga CI töö jaoks käivitab see ainulaadse alamvõrgu ja mahuga värske Infinito DinD konteineri, käivitab selle sees töö ja rebib selle alla; jooksja registreerib seejärel uuesti GitHubiga värske üürikese jooksjana."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every runner instance is an ephemeral container that mounts its host’s docker socket (DooD). For each CI job it starts a fresh Infinito DinD container with a unique subnet and volume, runs the job inside it, and tears it down; the runner then re-registers with GitHub as a fresh ephemeral runner."
msgstr "Iga jooksja eksemplar on üürike konteiner, mis paigaldab oma võõrustaja dokkimispesa. (DooD). Iga CI töö jaoks käivitab see ainulaadse alamvõrgu ja mahuga värske Infinito DinD konteineri, käivitab selle sees töö ja rebib selle alla; jooksja registreerib seejärel uuesti GitHubiga värske üürikese jooksjana."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every scenario MUST end with the browser in a clearly logged-out state."
msgstr "Iga stsenaarium peab lõppema brauseriga selgelt välja logitud olekus."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every selected run is attempted before anything is reported; abandoning the rest on the first rejection would leave them burning runners. `HTTP 409` means the run already finished and is not a rejection at all. Any other rejection is logged as an `ERROR` line, but only a denied token fails the job — a rate limit or a run that vanished between listing and cancel is transient, and a red check for those is a red check nobody reads."
msgstr "Iga valitud jooksu proovitakse enne, kui midagi teatatakse; ülejäänud loobumine esimesel tagasilükkamisel jätaks nad jooksjad põletama. `HTTP 409` See tähendab, et jooks on juba lõppenud ja see ei ole üldse tagasilükkamine. Mis tahes muu tagasilükkamine logitakse kui `ERROR` rida, kuid ainult keelatud märk ebaõnnestub töö - määrapiirang või jooksu, mis kadus nimekirja kandmise ja tühistamise vahel, on mööduv ja nende punane kontroll on punane kontroll, mida keegi ei loe."

msgid "Every selection names every axis: role, variant, mode, onion state, distro and filesystem. Nothing is left to the rotation."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every service-dependent step uses `skipUnlessServiceEnabled(...)`. Direct `process.env` reads of `<NAME>_SERVICE_ENABLED` are forbidden."
msgstr "Iga teenusest sõltuv samm kasutab `skipUnlessServiceEnabled(...)`. Otse. `process.env` loeb `<NAME>_SERVICE_ENABLED` on keelatud."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every shell invocation the agent makes: `make` targets, `git`/`gh`/`docker` calls, `grep`/`head`/`tail`/`wc`, Python test runners, log-capture pipelines, etc."
msgstr "Kõik kestad, mida agent teeb: `make` sihtmärgid, `git`/`gh`/`docker` kõned, `grep`/`head`/`tail`/`wc`, Pythoni katsejooksjad, palkide püüdmise torustikud jne"

# libretranslate
msgid "Every spec MUST include the three persona scenarios below as its baseline. Additional scenarios (RBAC loops, peer-to-peer messaging, federation round-trips, CSP-deep-checks, …) MAY be added on top. Three personas exist in the deploy fixture: `guest` (no Keycloak account), `biber` (regular end-user), and `administrator` (operator/admin). The flow shape is identical across roles. Only the role-specific selectors and the post-login assertion change. Service-dependent steps MUST be guarded with [`skipUnlessServiceEnabled('<svc>')`](../../../../../roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/service-gating.js) so a deploy with `disable=<svc>` reports the affected step as `skipped: <NAME>_SERVICE_ENABLED=false`, never `failed`."
msgstr "Iga spekter PEAB sisaldama oma lähtejoonena kolme allpool toodud persona stsenaariumi. Täiendavad stsenaariumid (RBAC silmused, peer-to-peer sõnumid, föderatsiooni edasi-tagasi reisid, CSP-sügav kontroll, ...) Võib lisada peale. Arendusseadmes on kolm isikut: `guest` (Keycloaki konto), `biber` (regulaarne lõppkasutaja)ja `administrator` (käitaja/haldur)Voolu kuju on kõigis rollides ühesugune. Muutuvad ainult rollispetsiifilised valijad ja sisselogimisjärgne väide. Teenusest sõltuvaid samme tuleb valvata [`skipUnlessServiceEnabled('<svc>')`](../../../../../roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/service-gating.js) lähetus `disable=<svc>` teatab mõjutatud etapist `skipped: <NAME>_SERVICE_ENABLED=false`, mitte kunagi `failed`."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Every spec MUST set `test.use({ ignoreHTTPSErrors: true })` at the top of the file because the test environment uses self-signed certificates. The central `playwright.config.js` does NOT set this globally. Per-spec opt-in is the contract."
msgstr "Iga komplekt PEAB `test.use({ ignoreHTTPSErrors: true })` faili ülaosas, sest katsekeskkonnas kasutatakse ise allkirjastatud sertifikaate. Keskne `playwright.config.js` See ei sea seda globaalselt paika. Perspect opt-in on leping."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every stack has its own domain below it (`INFINITO_DOMAIN`): the primary checkout is `main.infinito.test`, a worktree from `make worktree-up` is its branch lowercased with every character outside `a-z0-9_-` replaced by `-` (`feature/store-i18n` → `feature-store-i18n.infinito.test`). `linux.sh` routes each stack's domain to that checkout's `INFINITO_BIND_IP`, read from the `.env` of every `git worktree list` entry. Re-run `make network-dns-setup` after creating or removing a worktree."
msgstr "Igal korstnal on selle all oma domeen. (`INFINITO_DOMAIN`): esmane kassatsioon on `main.infinito.test`, tööpuu `make worktree-up` on tema haru, mis on iga väljaspool asuva märgiga `a-z0-9_-` asendatud `-` (`feature/store-i18n` → `feature-store-i18n.infinito.test`). `linux.sh` Teeb iga hunniku domeeni selle kassasse `INFINITO_BIND_IP`, lugeda `.env` igast `git worktree list` sissepääs. Käivita uuesti `make network-dns-setup` pärast tööpuu loomist või eemaldamist."

msgid "Every stateful role in the repo keeps both modes on; only host-level and infrastructure roles disable swarm. See [deployment-modes.md](../contributing/design/deployment-modes.md)."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Every sweep exercises both architectures across the catalogue instead of proving amd64 and claiming nothing, at no extra job count."
msgstr "Iga pühkimine kasutab mõlemat arhitektuuri kogu kataloogis, selle asemel, et tõestada64 Ja mitte midagi, ilma lisatööta."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every task that creates a new file."
msgstr "Iga ülesanne, mis loob uue faili."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every task that inspects a file."
msgstr "Iga ülesanne, mis kontrollib faili."

# libretranslate
msgid "Every task that modifies an existing file."
msgstr "Iga ülesanne, mis muudab olemasolevat faili."

