msgstr "OpenClaw tarbib MCP-d. Iga jagatud MCP serveri roll avastatakse ``MCP_DISCOVERED_SERVERS`` See on kirjutatud agendi konfiguratsiooni."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw exposes no administrator-visible list of configured MCP servers, so the configured set is proven by a CLI test instead: [`files/test/test.sh`](./files/test/test.sh) probes the agent's `mcp` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a `failed to start server` line. The Playwright spec covers the complementary case, that the gateway holding the MCP credentials refuses an unauthenticated caller."
msgstr "OpenClaw ei näita seadistatud MCP-serverite administraatorile nähtavat loendit, seega konfigureeritud kogum tõestatakse CLI testiga: [`files/test/test.sh`](./files/test/test.sh) sondib agendi `mcp` pinnale ja ebaõnnestub, kui exec ise ebaõnnestub või väljund kannab `failed to start server` joon. Playwrighti spetsifikatsioon hõlmab täiendavat juhtumit, et MCP mandaadiga värav keeldub autentimata helistajast."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw exposes no administrator-visible list of configured MCP servers, so the configured set is proven by a CLI test instead: ```files/test/test.sh`` <./files/test/test.sh>`__ probes the agent’s ``mcp`` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a ``failed to start server`` line. The Playwright spec covers the complementary case, that the gateway holding the MCP credentials refuses an unauthenticated caller."
msgstr "OpenClaw ei näita seadistatud MCP-serverite administraatorile nähtavat loendit, seega konfigureeritud kogum tõestatakse CLI testiga: ```files/test/test.sh`` <./files/test/test.sh>`__ probes the agent’s ``mcp`` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a ``failed to start server`` joon. Playwrighti spetsifikatsioon hõlmab täiendavat juhtumit, et MCP mandaadiga värav keeldub autentimata helistajast."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw's own CLI reference says so directly: `openclaw mcp serve` \"starts a stdio MCP server\" whose process \"the MCP client owns\". Every HTTP transport in that document belongs to the opposite direction, `openclaw mcp add --url --transport streamable-http`, which is OpenClaw acting as a client. Hermes is the same shape: both entry points, `mcp_serve.py` and `agent/transports/hermes_tools_mcp_server.py`, run the MCP SDK's stdio transport, the repository defines neither `run_streamable_http_async` nor `sse_app`, and the user-facing MCP guide describes only Hermes consuming external servers."
msgstr "OpenClawi enda CLI viide ütleb nii otse: `openclaw mcp serve` \"Stdio MCP serveri käivitamine\" kelle protsess \"MCP klient kuulub\"Iga HTTP-transport selles dokumendis kuulub vastupidisesse suunda. `openclaw mcp add --url --transport streamable-http`, mis on OpenClaw, kes tegutseb kliendina. Hermes on sama kuju: mõlemad sisenemispunktid, `mcp_serve.py` ja `agent/transports/hermes_tools_mcp_server.py`, käitab MCP SDK standardtransporti, hoidla ei määratle kumbagi `run_streamable_http_async` ega `sse_app`, ja kasutaja poole MCP juhend kirjeldab ainult Hermes tarbivad välised serverid."

