# libretranslate
msgid "When NO primary app ships a `meta/variants.yml`, the planner falls back to this path — the `CombinedResolver` walks `dependencies` and `shared:`-edges in the variant-merged services map and Jinja flags are evaluated at deploy time against `group_names`. `run_after` is NOT followed for inclusion (it is a pure ordering hint), so a variant that disables a service does not get the provider re-added through the ordering edge. This module owns the include resolution that path needs and nothing else; the round's variant-merged services maps come from `utils.roles.applications.variants`, which the CI selection resolves its closure from as well."
msgstr "Kui NO esmane rakendus saadab a `meta/variants.yml`, See tähendab, et planeerija pöördub tagasi sellele teele – `CombinedResolver` kõnnib `dependencies` ja `shared:`variandiga ühendatud teenuste kaardi servad ja Jinja lipud hinnatakse käivitusajal `group_names`. `run_after` ei ole lisatud (see on puhas tellimise vihje), nii et variant, mis keelab teenuse, ei saa teenusepakkujat uuesti lisada läbi tellimise serva. Sellel moodulil on kaasamisresolutsioon, mida rada vajab ja ei midagi muud; vooru variandiga ühendatud teenuste kaardid pärinevad `utils.roles.applications.variants`, mille ühenduse tootmisharu valik lahendab ka selle sulgemise."

