msgid "[`roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.sh) proves the endpoint answers its declared contract, not that any particular client can route to it: it runs in a throwaway container joined to the *provider's* own network, because an `expose:`-only endpoint resolves nowhere else. Per-client routing is therefore still unproven by any test. Measured by hand on compose, Open WebUI resolves `baserow` to `192.168.206.4` and `homeassistant` to `192.168.79.2`, both distinct from the wildcard address, so the topology carries those two pairs; Swarm is unmeasured. [`isolation.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/isolation.sh) does cover the adapter half, counting networks inside the sidecar for every `implementation: adapter` provider."
msgstr "[`roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.sh) tõestab, et lõpp-punkt vastab deklareeritud lepingule, mitte sellele, et mõni konkreetne klient saab selle juurde minna: see jookseb äravisatud konteineris, mis on ühendatud *varustaja* oma võrku, sest `expose:`Ainult lõpp-punkt ei lahenda kusagil mujal. Seetõttu ei ole ükski katse veel tõestanud kliendipõhist marsruuti. Mõõdetuna käsitsi komposel, Open WebUI lahendab `baserow` kuni `192.168.206.4` ja `homeassistant` kuni `192.168.79.2`, mõlemad erinevad metamärgi aadressist, nii et topoloogia kannab neid kahte paari; Swarm on mõõtmatu. [`isolation.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/isolation.sh) katab adapteri poole, loendades külgkorvis olevaid võrke iga `implementation: adapter` varustaja."

