# libretranslate
msgid "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` : Social Home 2026.6.16 imports `logout` from `client/src/store/auth.ts` in exactly one place —   `client/src/main.tsx` wires it as the 401 handler via `setUnauthorizedHandler(logout)`. No   component renders a logout control, so `personas/utils/logout.js` has nothing to click and the   admin journey cannot complete. The alternative — injecting a `[data-injected-logout]` button via   `templates/javascript.js.j2` — was rejected: the model   (`roles/web-app-prometheus/templates/javascript.js.j2`) points the button at   `OIDC.CLIENT.LOGOUT_URL`, which only exists for OIDC-gated roles, and this role deliberately runs   without SSO. Path back: upstream ships a logout control (or an in-app logout endpoint we can   target), then drop the flag and keep the `adminInteraction` already wired in the spec."
msgstr "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` Sotsiaalkodu 2026.6.16 import `logout` pärit `client/src/store/auth.ts` täpselt ühes kohas – `client/src/main.tsx` traadid 401 käitleja `setUnauthorizedHandler(logout)`. Ükski komponent ei muuda väljalogimise juhtimist, nii et `personas/utils/logout.js` pole midagi klõpsata ja administraatori teekond ei saa lõpule viia. Alternatiiv – süstida `[data-injected-logout]` nupp `templates/javascript.js.j2` – lükati tagasi: mudel (`roles/web-app-prometheus/templates/javascript.js.j2`) osutab nupule `OIDC.CLIENT.LOGOUT_URL`, mis eksisteerib ainult OIDC-ga kaetud rollide jaoks ja see roll töötab tahtlikult ilma SSO-ta. Tagasitee: ülesvoolulaevad väljalogimisseade (või rakenduse sisselogimise lõpp-punkt, mida saame sihtida)siis heida lipp maha ja jäta `adminInteraction` juba traadiga."

# libretranslate
msgid "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` is declared because the shared helper cannot reach Shopware's logout, not because the journey is untestable. The only logout control lives in `.sw-admin-menu__user-actions`, which the administration stylesheet keeps at `display: none` until its toggle is clicked, and that toggle is a bare `div` carrying no role, no `aria-haspopup` and no dropdown class — nothing in the helper's trigger set matches it. Its second fallback, following a same-origin settings link, misses as well because the administration is hash-routed and every settings target is `#/sw/settings/...`."
msgstr "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` on deklareeritud, sest jagatud abimees ei jõua ShopwareMitte sellepärast, et reis oleks ebakindel. Ainus väljaräägi kontroll elab `.sw-admin-menu__user-actions`, mida halduse laadileht hoiab `display: none` kuni selle lülitamine on klõpsatud ja see lülitamine on tühi `div` rollita, ei `aria-haspopup` Ja ei mingit dropdown klassi - midagi abistaja päästiku komplekti sobib. Selle teine varuvariant, mis järgneb sama päritoluga seadete lingile, jääb ka vahele, sest administratsioon on räsisuunatud ja iga seade sihtmärk on `#/sw/settings/...`."

# libretranslate
msgid "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` is declared for a second, independent reason, and two separate obstacles justify it."
msgstr "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` on kuulutatud teisel, sõltumatul põhjusel ja seda õigustavad kaks eraldi takistust."

# libretranslate
msgid "`PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` : The app authenticates against its own `platform_users` table. There is no OIDC client and no   auto-provisioning, so the biber account never exists inside Social Home. Path back: upstream   grows an OIDC/trusted-header auth path."
msgstr "`PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` : rakendus autentib enda vastu `platform_users` laud. Puudub OIDC klient ja automaatne pakkumine, nii et Biberi konto ei eksisteeri kunagi sees. Social Home. Tee tagasi: ülesvoolu kasvab OIDC/trusted-header autth tee."

