# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant kuvab märgi kontole, mis selle vermis. See kasutuselevõtt vermib selle administraatorile, nii et kõne saabub administraatorina, kes kliendilt küsis. Üksuse riskipositsioon piirab endiselt ulatust. Tööriistaserverisse jõudmine on väravas rollis ``mcp`` RBAC grupp."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost piirab kõne kontoga, millele märk kuulub. See kasutuselevõtt vermib selle administraatorikonto isikliku juurdepääsu, nii et kõned saabuvad selle konto õigustega, kes küsis. Tööriistaserverisse jõudmine on väravas rollis ``mcp`` RBAC grupp."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: API token väljastatakse administraatori konto vastu, nii et iga kõne kannab selle konto õigusi olenemata sellest, kes küsis kliendilt. Tööriistaserverisse jõudmine on väravas rollis ``mcp`` RBAC grupp, mis on eraldiseisev toetus haldamisest Jenkins."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: isikliku juurdepääsu luba on vermitud vastu ``root`` konto ja mida hoitakse ``administrator`` Iga kõne kannab selle konto õigusi olenemata sellest, kes kliendilt küsis. Tööriistaserverisse jõudmine on väravas rollis ``mcp`` RBAC grupp, mis on eraldiseisev toetus haldamisest GitLab."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Veebiteenuse märgis väljastatakse administraatori konto vastu, nii et kõne kannab selle konto õigusi olenemata sellest, kes kliendilt küsis. Lisatud funktsioonid on kirjutuskaitstud, mis piirab seda, mida need õigused siin teha saavad. Tööriistaserverisse jõudmine on väravas rollis ``mcp`` RBAC grupp."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Helistatakse Baserow lõpp-punkti omanikuna, olenemata sellest, kes küsis kliendilt, ja jõuab ainult ühele tööruumile, mis kontole kuulub. See on adapteri lubatud nimekirja teine limiit, mitte selle asendaja."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBACi kontsern, mis on eraldiseisev toetus Nextcloud konto."

# libretranslate
