# libretranslate
msgid "``poll: 0`` makes a task fire and forget, so its own ``changed_when`` and ``failed_when`` never see an outcome. The outcome only exists once the job is collected with ``async_status``, and collecting it is where the verdict has to be made -- for a whole batch at once, so one run reports every broken job rather than the first."
msgstr "``poll: 0`` Paneb ülesande põlema ja unustab, nii et oma ``changed_when`` ja ``failed_when`` ei näe kunagi tulemust. Tulemus on olemas ainult siis, kui töö on kogutud ``async_status``, Ja selle kogumine on koht, kus kohtuotsus tuleb teha - kogu partii kohta korraga, nii et üks käik teatab igast katkisest tööst, mitte esimesest."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ports.onion`` is a category-keyed map of booleans alongside ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: it names which of a service's already-declared ports should answer on the node onion, and nothing else. The port number comes from ``ports.local`` when that category is declared there and from ``ports.public`` otherwise, which is the precedence ``container_ports`` publishes by, so the forward always targets the port the service is actually reachable on."
msgstr "``ports.onion`` on booleanide kategooriakaart kõrvuti ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: See nimetab, milline teenuse juba deklareeritud sadamatest peaks vastama sõlme sibulale ja mitte midagi muud. Port number pärineb ``ports.local`` Kui see kategooria on seal deklareeritud ja ``ports.public`` muidu, mis on pretsedent ``container_ports`` avaldab, nii et edasipääs on alati suunatud sadamale, kus teenus on tegelikult kättesaadav."

